(242537, 14681, 6870, '<td valign="top">I like the position of the fish here; they make nice lines, and you''ve managed to capture the scales of the larger fish in some detail. The other fish seems overexposed, perhaps because  you used a flash. You might try taking a similar shot with lights rather than a flash, or fiddle more with your levels in Photoshop (if that''s what you use) to even the tones.</td>', 'I like the position of the fish here; they make nice lines, and you''ve managed to capture the scales of the larger fish in some detail. The other fish seems overexposed, perhaps because  you used a flash. You might try taking a similar shot with lights rather than a flash, or fiddle more with your levels in Photoshop (if that''s what you use) to even the tones.', '2003-03-21 02:02:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(242539, 14597, 6870, '<td valign="top">Cute dog; you''ve a good eye for animal expression! The image is drastically out of focus, though. If you have a macro setting on your camera, that might solve the focus problem, as this is somewhat close.</td>', 'Cute dog; you''ve a good eye for animal expression! The image is drastically out of focus, though. If you have a macro setting on your camera, that might solve the focus problem, as this is somewhat close.', '2003-03-21 02:03:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(242541, 14768, 6870, '<td valign="top">Interesting frozen position of this cat. I like the B/W here. The cat is out of focus, though. The negative space at the right is a good counterpoint for the bizarre cat.</td>', 'Interesting frozen position of this cat. I like the B/W here. The cat is out of focus, though. The negative space at the right is a good counterpoint for the bizarre cat.', '2003-03-21 02:04:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(242542, 14449, 6870, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, and the hoop looks good in the center. The whole image is grainy and out of focus for no reason that I can see. Try focusing first on the subject by pressing the button half way, then move your camera to compose the picture while still holding the button. Viola, your subject will be in focus.</td>', 'I like the idea, and the hoop looks good in the center. The whole image is grainy and out of focus for no reason that I can see. Try focusing first on the subject by pressing the button half way, then move your camera to compose the picture while still holding the button. Viola, your subject will be in focus.', '2003-03-21 02:07:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(242543, 14416, 6870, '<td valign="top">I like the composition of this shot in terms of arrangement. The tree on the left give the image some weight and grounds it with some negative space (kind of). The whole image is out of focus, though. Also, for shots like this in daytime light, try your smallest aperture, and don''t compensate for reciprocity failure. Your image will often take on more interesting light.</td>', 'I like the composition of this shot in terms of arrangement. The tree on the left give the image some weight and grounds it with some negative space (kind of). The whole image is out of focus, though. Also, for shots like this in daytime light, try your smallest aperture, and don''t compensate for reciprocity failure. Your image will often take on more interesting light.', '2003-03-21 02:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(242548, 14450, 6172, '<td valign="top">True, it is blurry.  I can''t score it too highly, as you would suspect.  There are interesting patterns on the asphalt there.</td>', 'True, it is blurry.  I can''t score it too highly, as you would suspect.  There are interesting patterns on the asphalt there.', '2003-03-21 02:37:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(242549, 14286, 6172, '<td valign="top">It''s a very nice photo with nice colors.  I am wondering how many comments you are getting on how it is not demonstrated by the photo that you have taken the shot "From Above"?</td>', 'It''s a very nice photo with nice colors.  I am wondering how many comments you are getting on how it is not demonstrated by the photo that you have taken the shot "From Above"?', '2003-03-21 02:38:57.000000', NULL, 1),
